&lt;p>The coordinate system we use most is the standard Cartesian plane right-angle coordinate system, which takes the lower-left corner of the screen as the origin and increases the y coordinate upwards and the x coordinate to the right.&lt;/p>
&lt;p>SCWindow&amp;rsquo;s coordinates, on the other hand, are flipped coordinates with the upper-left corner of the main screen as the origin, and the following is a simple comparison chart:&lt;/p>
&lt;p>&lt;img loading="lazy" src="https://travisbikkle.github.io/images/posts/make-mactoys/flip-coordinate.png" alt="alt text" srcset="https://travisbikkle.github.io/images/posts/make-mactoys/flip-coordinate.png?size=small, https://travisbikkle.github.io/images/posts/make-mactoys/flip-coordinate.png?size=medium 1.5x, https://travisbikkle.github.io/images/posts/make-mactoys/flip-coordinate.png?size=large 2x" data-title="alt text" style="--width: 424px;--aspect-ratio: 424 / 848;background: url(/images/loading.min.svg) no-repeat center;" onload="this.title=this.dataset.title;for(const i of ['style', 'data-title','onerror','onload']){this.removeAttribute(i);}this.dataset.lazyloaded='';" onerror="this.title=this.dataset.title;for(const i of ['style', 'data-title','onerror','onload']){this.removeAttribute(i);}"/>&lt;/p></description></item></channel></rss>